  "description": "Codex: Orks (11e) GROT SHIELDS (Runt Swarm, 1 CP) through the real enemy_targets_unit_shooting fold-in of the defender's reactive StratagemDialog, together with the core SMOKESCREEN in the SAME targeting (several reactive stratagems per targeting). Fixture ork11e_orks_reactive: P1 Custodes ACTIVE, P2 Orks. Setup-only privileges: P2's detachment is flipped to Runt Swarm and its stratagems reloaded; the Kommandos (SMOKE) are moved into Custodian Guard C's range. The Custodes player selects Custodian Guard C by clicking its token and splits its guardian spears between the Flash Gitz, the Tankbustas and the Kommandos (phase actions the shooting panel sends). The Ork player's dialog offers GROT SHIELDS on Gretchin C (within 3\" of BOTH targeted Flash Gitz and Tankbustas, so a second pick is needed) and SMOKESCREEN on the Kommandos. Real clicks: Use on Gretchin C -> the unit picker asks which unit to shield -> Flash Gitz (1 CP); the dialog RE-OPENS with SMOKESCREEN only (GROT SHIELDS is once per phase) -> Use on Kommandos (1 CP more). The attack then resolves (dock Fast Roll / Complete Shooting): every hit on the Flash Gitz is intercepted by a Gretchin model, which suffers a mortal wound instead, so the Flash Gitz end unharmed while Gretchin C loses models.",
